From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] hijack: Set a plain window's D-Bus properties once it is
 realized

On Wayland the window data of a window that is not a GtkApplicationWindow
was made before the realize was chained up to. Making it calls
gdk_wayland_window_set_dbus_properties_libgtk_only with the widget's
GdkWindow, which a widget has only once it is realized, so the call
failed its GDK_IS_WAYLAND_WINDOW assertion and the compositor was never
told where the menu is. The data was kept, so nothing tried again. A
program with a GtkMenuBar in a plain GtkWindow, as mate-terminal and
mate-calc have, exported a menu that nothing could find.

Make the data after the realize, as the X11 branch does. A
GtkApplicationWindow keeps its own order: GTK reads the application's
menubar while it realizes the window.
---
 subprojects/appmenu-gtk-module/src/hijack.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/subprojects/appmenu-gtk-module/src/hijack.c b/subprojects/appmenu-gtk-module/src/hijack.c
index 0bb1d78..98c88b6 100644
--- a/subprojects/appmenu-gtk-module/src/hijack.c
+++ b/subprojects/appmenu-gtk-module/src/hijack.c
@@ -78,16 +78,16 @@
 	if (visual && (hint == GDK_WINDOW_TYPE_HINT_DND))
 		gtk_widget_set_visual(widget, visual);
 
-// In Wayland the DBUS Menu need to be register before realize the window.
+	if (pre_hijacked_window_realize != NULL)
+		pre_hijacked_window_realize(widget);
+
+// A plain GtkWindow has no GdkWindow to set the D-Bus properties on until it's realized.
 #ifdef GDK_WINDOWING_WAYLAND
 	if (GDK_IS_WAYLAND_DISPLAY(gdk_display_get_default()) && is_hint_viable &&
 	    (!GTK_IS_APPLICATION_WINDOW(GTK_WINDOW(widget))))
 		gtk_window_get_window_data(GTK_WINDOW(widget));
 #endif
 
-	if (pre_hijacked_window_realize != NULL)
-		pre_hijacked_window_realize(widget);
-
 #ifdef GDK_WINDOWING_X11
 	if (is_hint_viable
 #if GTK_MAJOR_VERSION == 3
